{"id":"multiprocessing.shared_memory/ShareableList","module":"multiprocessing.shared_memory","qualname":"ShareableList","name":"ShareableList","kind":"class","parent":null,"signatures":["ShareableList(sequence=None, *, name=None)"],"doc":"Pattern for a mutable list-like object shareable via a shared\nmemory block.  It differs from the built-in list type in that these\nlists can not change their overall length (i.e. no append, insert,\netc.)\n\nBecause values are packed into a memoryview as bytes, the struct\npacking format for any storable value must require no more than 8\ncharacters to describe its format.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/multiprocessing.shared_memory.html#multiprocessing.shared_memory.ShareableList","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":[],"source":{"path":"Lib/multiprocessing/shared_memory.py","line":259},"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
