{"id":"multiprocessing.shared_memory/SharedMemory.unlink","module":"multiprocessing.shared_memory","qualname":"SharedMemory.unlink","name":"unlink","kind":"method","parent":"multiprocessing.shared_memory/SharedMemory","signatures":["SharedMemory.unlink()"],"doc":"Requests that the underlying shared memory block be destroyed.\n\nUnlink should be called once (and only once) across all handles\nwhich have access to the shared memory block, even if these\nhandles belong to different processes. Closing and unlinking may\nhappen in any order, but trying to access data inside a shared\nmemory block after unlinking may result in memory errors,\ndepending on platform.\n\nThis method has no effect on Windows, where the only way to\ndelete a shared memory block is to close all handles.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/multiprocessing.shared_memory.html#multiprocessing.shared_memory.SharedMemory.unlink","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":[],"source":{"path":"Lib/multiprocessing/shared_memory.py","line":238},"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false}
